{"title":"2010 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 13","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Angelina drove at an average rate of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/a/fea5fcc6d66685ee21f722efcd228eb44d38f262.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$80$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> kmh and then stopped <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> minutes for gas. After the stop, she drove at an average rate of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> kmh. Altogether she drove <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/8/448b3c8f2596d1b93b4b3ef199f8b3241ced9da2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$250$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> km in a total trip time of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> hours including the stop. Which equation could be used to solve for the time <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" /> in hours that she drove before her stop?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/8/0187ebf903af816c830f075d0b39e5fad2ac7828.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 80t+100\\left(\\frac{8}{3}-t\\right)=250 \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 80t=250 \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 100t=250 \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 90t=250 \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 80\\left(\\frac{8}{3}-t\\right)+100t=250$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"934\" height=\"43\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> because she drove at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/a/fea5fcc6d66685ee21f722efcd228eb44d38f262.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$80$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> kmh for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" /> hours (the amount of time before the stop), and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> kmh for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/9/7b99a48cc084784eba58040490a868641b774869.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{8}{3}-t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"41\" height=\"37\" /> because she wasn't driving for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> minutes, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/1/4e1965f8d70832ded66434c75a7bd52b75090af0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> hours. Multiplying by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" /> gives the total distance, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/8/448b3c8f2596d1b93b4b3ef199f8b3241ced9da2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$250$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> km. Therefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/3/493e479cb8b73a1f86ab2c80756e56e0b3432e6d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$80t+100\\left(\\frac{8}{3}-t\\right)=250$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"196\" height=\"43\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/3/843622567e12d686e4e2f94ddfcb444e8ecde0d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Rightarrow$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"9\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/4/70432e471002b1c1f363f2d085b0f3dff8d930a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{(A)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"39\" height=\"29\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A\" title=\"2010 AMC 10A\">2010 AMC 10A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2010 AMC 10A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2010 AMC 10A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_12\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2010 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 12\">Problem 12</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_14\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2010 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 14\">Problem 14</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2010 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2010 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2010 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2010 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2010 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2010 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2010 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2010 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_9\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2010 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2010 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem